**Visualization for both perimeters**

Use `.plot()` to get a preliminary view on both the fire perimeters.

::: {#b4c6d040 .cell execution_count=5}
``` {.python .cell-code}
fig, (ax1, ax2) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(7,7))

# Remove the axis for a cleaner map
ax1.axis('off')
ax2.axis('off')

# Plot Eaton
eaton.plot(ax=ax1, color="cornflowerblue", linewidth=2.5, edgecolor="navy")
ax1.set_title('Eaton Perimeter',
             fontsize=14, weight='bold', pad=15)

# Plot Palisades
palisades.plot(ax=ax2, color="cornflowerblue", linewidth=2.5, edgecolor="gold")
ax2.set_title('Palisades Perimeter',
             fontsize=14, weight='bold', pad=15)
plt.tight_layout()
plt.show()
```

